<concept base="Anywhere" id="t00803">
	<title>Recommended cold tire inflation pressures</title>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e05126">
								<title>Type A</title>
								<figgroup>
									<image href="../../images/OOV085003.eps" align="center" height="1.740in" placement="break" id="e05127"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2">
							<fig id="fig_m1w_k3s_n3c">
								<title>Type B</title>
								<figgroup>
									<image href="../../images/OOV085002.eps" align="center" height="1.740in" placement="break" id="image_n1w_k3s_n3c"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>All specifications (sizes and pressures) can be found on a label attached to the vehicle.</p>
		<note type="tip">
			<p>All tire pressures should be checked when the tires are cold. “Cold Tires” means the vehicle has not been driven for at least three hours or driven less than 1.6 km (1 mile).</p>
		</note>
	</conbody>
</concept>